{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And Moses did… so they did.</b> One must examine why it repeats, saying <b>as He commanded… so they did</b> — the verse should have sufficed with one of them. It appears that it intends to say that they carried out the mission exactly as HaShem had spoken to them, on two levels: first, that everything they grasped from the words of HaShem, that is exactly what they did; second, that they intended toward the truth of the matter with completeness. And this is the measure of the verse: ״וַיַּעַשׂ מֹשֶׁה וְגוֹ׳ כַּאֲשֶׁר צִוָּה״ and so forth — and they did not change a thing; and the verse returns and testifies and says <b>as HaShem commanded them</b> — meaning, what HaShem intended in His commandment to them, that they did. Understand this." "<b>Further,</b> it intends to say that every act of Moses and Aaron was not for the sake of any intermediary cause, but solely because HaShem commanded them — and this is along the lines of the verse's saying (Deuteronomy 6:25) ״וּצְדָקָה תִּהְיֶה לָנוּ וְגוֹ׳ כַּאֲשֶׁר צִוָּנוּ״, and His saying <b>so they did</b> refers to the act itself, that it was done without any change." "<b>Further,</b> it intends that for each and every utterance they would mention the Name of Heaven, and this is His saying <b>they did</b>, and at the time of the act they said ״כַּאֲשֶׁר״ and so forth. Further, it intends to say that they did not delay in the matter, but immediately and instantaneously, as soon as HaShem finished commanding them, they hastened to do the word of HaShem."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:25:26.549046409Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}